  "authoringNote": "The final order f26b-order v1 states order date 2026-09-04 and order timestamp 2026-09-04T09:30:00-07:00 with time zone America/Los_Angeles, which is 2026-09-04T16:30:00Z; no zone is inferred. The single receipt f26b-receipt v1 references that exact order version and states receivedAt 2026-09-04T16:29:59Z, one second before the stated order timestamp. The receipt also lies inside the date span 2026-09-03T10:00:00Z to 2026-09-05T12:00:00Z, but under C06 a receipt before the stated timestamp is certainly before the order. The receipt is current, usable and linked, so R05 is conflict for the administrative reviewer with only R05.receipt_before_order, naming [f26b-order v1, f26b-receipt v1] in canonical order. No receipt candidate, R05.order_receipt_missing or absence condition holds. R05 cites the receipt order document ID, order version and receivedAt and the order date and timestamp (five). R04 passes: the encounter date 2026-08-26 differs from the order date, so the order time settles nothing under C02; R04 cites the encounter status, date and practitioner identifier and the order status, date, timestamp and practitioner identifier (seven; the null completion time supplies no fact). R02 passes citing the beneficiary name and identifier of the encounter, the order and the receipt (six). The rest follows the supported packet, checked by hand: the final encounter (2026-08-26) and the final signed order (2026-09-04) both name practitioner identifier SYN-PRAC-0001; the order is after the encounter, on a different date, and within the inclusive C01 bound 2027-02-26; the order item code K0823 equals the case; the named supplier record f26b-supplier-status v1 is usable and states non_exempt, established, no new enrollment, no ownership change and the interval 2026-01-01 to 2026-12-31, which contains the assessment date 2026-10-18. R01 passes citing the seven supplier record facts and the order item code; R03 passes citing the nine order facts. R06 stays manual_review for the qualified clinical reviewer with R06.clinical_review and the five full /clinical/ pointers; it neither blocks nor satisfies readiness and draws no medical necessity conclusion. R07 passes citing the stated LCMP flag false (the null evaluation date supplies no fact); no ATP, specialty, home assessment or proof-of-delivery item is required. R08 passes on the reviewed pack and the supported date. R10 is not_applicable with R10.pure_assessment. clinicalReviewRequired is true. R09 passes. The state is needs_human_review from R05 alone. Quarantine and superseded lists are empty, and every parent affectedDocuments set is empty: the order and receipt are named only at condition level (C07).",
